https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3092#issuecomment-448357055"},"message":"@bpoldrack have you tried opening the file in a text editor?\n\n`cat`ing it will echo the `\\r` to the terminal, which will be interpreted as a carriage return, and the next line will overwrite it but it'll happen quickly enough that you can't see it.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1545167904,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0ODM2NzIwMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3092#issuecomment-448367202"},"message":"\u003e @bpoldrack have you tried opening the file in a text editor?\n\nI did when I tried the `create` snippet and didn't see any control sequences.  Looks like its version dependent.\n\nContents (not what the terminal displays) on master (07b952c): \n\n```\n# datalad create $(mktemp -d) \u003eout 2\u003e\u0026\n[INFO] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/tmp.Gl4Js4brOs \ncreate(ok): /tmp/tmp.Gl4Js4brOs (dataset)\n```\n\nAnd on the version you report, v0.10.1:\n\n```\n[INFO] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/tmp.QI4hVZ3hQo \n^MTotal:   0%|          | 0.00/21.0 [00:00\u003c?, ?B/s]^M                                                 ^MTotal:   0%|          | 0.00/250 [00:00\u003c?, ?B/s]^M                                                ^Mcreate(ok): /tmp/tmp.QI4hVZ3hQo (dataset)\n```\n\nThat bisects to the merge commit 2517f6146 (Merge pull request #2749 from mih/rf-generator, 2018-08-15).  I don't yet understand why the merge doesn't show the progress output while both parents do.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1545167904,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE2Mzk5NTYxMQ=="},"target":"2910b29b49374a1ab37eafbd919b4773596da242f299bbffe67567cd97850693","message":"\u003e @bpoldrack have you tried opening the file in a text editor?\n\nI did when I tried the `create` snippet and didn't see any control sequences.  Looks like it's version dependent.\n\nContents (not what the terminal displays) on master (07b952c): \n\n```\n# datalad create $(mktemp -d) \u003eout 2\u003e\u0026\n[INFO] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/tmp.Gl4Js4brOs \ncreate(ok): /tmp/tmp.Gl4Js4brOs (dataset)\n```\n\nAnd on the version you report, v0.10.1:\n\n```\n[INFO] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/tmp.QI4hVZ3hQo \n^MTotal:   0%|          | 0.00/21.0 [00:00\u003c?, ?B/s]^M                                                 ^MTotal:   0%|          | 0.00/250 [00:00\u003c?, ?B/s]^M                                                ^Mcreate(ok): /tmp/tmp.QI4hVZ3hQo (dataset)\n```\n\nThat bisects to the merge commit 2517f6146 (Merge pull request #2749 from mih/rf-generator, 2018-08-15).  I don't yet understand why the merge doesn't show the progress output while both parents do.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1553718268,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ3NzMzMzE4NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3092#issuecomment-477333184"},"message":"I said\n\n\u003e That bisects to the merge commit 2517f6146 (Merge pull request #2749 from mih/rf-generator, 2018-08-15).  I don't yet understand why the merge doesn't show the progress output while both parents\ndo.\n\nThat bisect looks like nonsense.  I'm having no luck triggering the `create` progress bars now.  On any version I've tried, I don't see progress bars when using `datalad create $(mktemp -d) \u003eout 2\u003e\u00261`.  Dunno.\n\nAnyway, any command that uses a progress bar from `ConsoleLog.get_progressbar` (like `download-url`, but not `create`) will show progress bars even with no tty attached.\n\n@yarikoptic says:\n\n\u003e I actually thought that we are disabling all the \"fancy\" UI elements such as progress bars in non-interactive runs... but then realized that probably we didn't since progress bars might be useful even then.\n\nRight, if `is_interactive` returns false, `ui` sets the backend to `ConsoleLog`, not `SilentConsoleLog`, so we'll still see progress bars.\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/52719b0e52628c1db912663fe3aad4ee6f06eb49/datalad/ui/__init__.py#L82\n\n\u003e But may be we should disable\n\nI'd vote for that (i.e. use `SilentConsoleLog` rather than `ConsoleLog` when `is_interactive` returns false).\n\n\u003e or change them to be minimalistic (e.g. progress bar just a growing sequence of .s  or so) indeed so we do not pollute the logs if output is not a tty.\n\nOr we could start using `log_progress` more.  That switches to using log messages to indicate progress when we're non-interactive.\n\nIn terms of this issue specifically, I think we can consider it resolved once we use `SilentConsoleLog` when non-interactive or at least make it possible to configure this.  Users should then be able to quiet the output to their liking by configuring log level/target and possibly `report_status`.\n\nBut stepping back a bit, the initial post said\n\n\u003e The specifics are about the progress bar, but the general complaint can be summarized as \"it should be easier to systematically parse the output when invoked in a script.\"\n\nDepending on what the specifics are here, rather than parsing the output it could be better to use the python api and deal with the result dictionaries.  You could also get theses records with `-f json` from the command line, but the progress bars when not attached to a tty would still be an issue in this case.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1554002971,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjI0MTM1MDQxMA=="},"status":2}]}